name: Ownership
tagline: "A seeded beneficial-ownership and sanctions Link Analysis demo - a hidden owner behind a 5-layer chain, a sanctioned person two hops from a customer, a nominee director of 120 companies and a circle of companies paying each other, planted among 6 000 companies and 5 000 people with benign look-alikes"
description: "The KYC and sanctions-compliance Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier. Seven synthetic feeds (company, person, ownership, officer, customer, payment, sanctions_list; a register snapshot and 12 months of payments from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, October 2026 and 8 new customers in data/staged; 6 000 companies, 5 000 people, 1 500 bank customers, about 40 000 payments and an INVENTED sanctions list of 400 people) are landed by seven Collectors and Pipelines. The ownership_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, percent, score, event_date, via) of five link kinds: owns, officer_of, customer_is, paid and name_match, a fuzzy match to the list (DuckDB jaro_winkler_similarity at 0.90 or above with the same birth year and nationality). Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-ownership-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by OwnershipLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-ownership-data.test.mjs): one person reaches 4 customers through a 5-layer chain across Cyprus, the British Virgin Islands and the UAE with every stake at 24 %, ending in 61 % of each customer; a customer's 50 % owner is 60 % owned by a person who matches a listed person; one person directs 120 companies at one formation-agent address; three companies own each other in a circle and pay each other round it every month. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: a listed company with widely held shares, a near-namesake of a listed person with a different birth year and nationality, an accountant directing 4 family firms, and a group with a clear parent. Four saved views, one per story. Basic tier: runs on every edition, Basic included. Advanced tier, in the same template and inert on Basic: Demo Users and roles (config/demo-users.toon, roles.toon: ownership.analyst lead, ownership.manager second approver, ownership.reviewer read-only, ownership.outsider not a member, admin), four-eyes above a fan-out of 2000 and Drafts (link-analysis.toon), the ownership_sanctions_counts and ownership_sanctions_alerts Jobs and the Alert Rule ownership_path_to_listed_person (an ownership path of 3 hops or fewer from a customer's company up to a person matched to the list; on the shipped data it counts one path, two hops above CUS-00528, one customer and one matched person - never the near-namesake, who owns a customer's company outright but is not matched; unarmed on Basic). Investigations, members, an Entity List, a Case, a held four-eyes expand and a Draft are runtime state: run `node tools/seed-la-ownership.mjs --apply` on an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth. Synthetic data only; no name on the sanctions list is real."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:building-office-2
contents[7]: "7 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (register snapshot, 12 months of payments landed, 1 month staged)", "ownership_links Job + Dataset (5 link kinds, percent, score, via)", "name_match by Jaro-Winkler against an invented sanctions list", "4 saved views (hidden owner, sanctions path, nominee director, circular ownership)", "4 planted stories with benign look-alikes", "Advanced tier: 5 Demo Users + role table, four-eyes (inert on Basic)", "Advanced tier: Alert Rule on an ownership path to a listed person within 3 hops (counts Job + evaluate Job, unarmed on Basic)"
